v 3
d sqldta: load a SQL Server table into a frame, with labels and notes from a label table
d
d sqldta loads a table or view from Microsoft SQL Server into a Stata frame
d over ODBC. It can apply value labels, variable labels, display formats,
d notes and a data label that are stored as rows of a label table in the same
d database, and can join a table whose columns are split across several
d tables. Its if qualifier takes a Stata expression, which it translates to
d T-SQL, so that only the matching rows are read from the server.
d
d The package includes sqldta_site_example.cfg, an example of the settings
d file sqldta_site.cfg; see help sqldta, Site configuration.
d
d Requires: Stata 16 or later (Stata 16 updated to 1 September 2020 or
d later), an ODBC driver for SQL Server, and databases with a
d case-insensitive collation, the default of SQL Server. Tested on Stata 18
d and 19.
d
d Author: Warren Holroyd
d Support: https://github.com/w4rhol/sqldta
d Licence: MIT
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261028
